comments.body:
After several failed attempts, I managed to complete this quest solo as a level 48 hunter.&nbsp; It was not easy, but I'll share some tips that I have learned (the hard way...)

I went with my wolf pet.&nbsp; His dps is a bit less than an offense-centric pet, but he seems to hold focus better, as bite only fires once every 10 seconds.&nbsp; This seems to give him more focus available for the all-vital growl.&nbsp; He has a few more HP and AC than my cat, so I thought that he might hold up a bit better on this quest.&nbsp; 

First, and perhaps key to the quest, is that you [b]HAVE[/b] to keep the witch doctor alive and chanting through TWO waves of gorillas.&nbsp; It is on the [b]third[/b] wave that Mokk spawns.&nbsp; There is a named gorilla in the second wave, but the heart is dropped on the third phase.&nbsp; You do [b]NOT[/b] need an alive-and-well witchdoctor after Mokk spawns.&nbsp; All you need to do is loot the heart for the completion of the quest.

The first wave wasn't too bad.&nbsp; They spawn outside the cave and come rushing in.&nbsp; I put my pet on them as soon as they appeared, trying to make sure he pulled as much aggro as possible.&nbsp; I kept assisting him until he needed to be healed.&nbsp; That, of course, produced some aggro on to me which was handled via feign death.&nbsp; I managed to clear the first wave with a healthy pet, but almost no mana remaining. 

Fortunately, there is a small pause before the second wave, and it spawns at a slightly greater distance from the cave than the first wave. This gave me time to drink part of a mana drink.&nbsp; I went with moonberry juice, which actually recharges my mana fairly quickly (I don't need to remain seated for the entire drink phase).

I dropped the pet on the named one in the second wave.&nbsp; I don't know if he was the highest level or not, but he was the first one that I targeted. I got FIVE gorillas on the second phase, and even though they were 5 levels less than me on average, that is still quite a challenge.&nbsp; Again, the issue was managing mana and pet health, and taking agro when needed.&nbsp; Even with decent gear, etc, my pet almost died during this round, and I was fairly beat up as well.&nbsp; 

That brought on the third round, which included our named friend and his all-valuable heart.&nbsp; Because I no longer needed the witch-doctor's services for chanting, I went with a change of plans... (He didn't realize it, I'm sure, but he was going to help in the fight).

A quick mana potion gave me enough to heal my pet to full.&nbsp; I let them come all the way into the cave, then dropped my pet on the named dude.&nbsp; I then got far enough away to pepper him with arrows.&nbsp; One feign was necessary to make sure I didn't have any aggro.&nbsp; Once the named one fell, I hit Aspect of Cheetah, put the pet on passive, and ran!&nbsp; The whole lot chased us for a while, then went back to beat-up the poor witch doctor...

This gave me enough time to re-group, heal my pet, and return to the fray.&nbsp; I think the good doctor took one of them out, because there were only three left, and the doc was wailing on one of them.&nbsp; I put my pet on the remaining ones long enough for me to loot and scamper.&nbsp; 

This was my fourth try at this darn quest, which is WAY under-rated in terms of level as far as I'm concerned.

[b]The CORDINATES ARE[/b]&nbsp; 
[pad][div align=center][b]~~~ 34 , 61 ~~~[/b][/div][pad]
I did solo it... but I was lvl 50. Be en garde.
